<title>EGYPT: Egypt housing firm '95/96 dividend up.</title>
<headline>Egypt housing firm '95/96 dividend up.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's United Housing and Development will give a 0.86 pound dividend for the 1995/6 financial year, up from 0.85 pounds in the previous year, published results showed on Monday.</p>
<p>The financial years end on June 30.</p>
<p>The partly-private firm also raised net after-tax profits to 4.81 million pounds ($1.41 million) for '95/96 from 4.73 million in financial 1994/5.</p>
<p>The partly private firm has 4,229,000 shares trading on the Egyptian stock exchange. The shares closed on Sunday at 22.70 pounds after heavy trade.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.4 Egyptian pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
